{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on c7a68450: the first script uses a local bare repository.\nP1 builds no authenticated connector.\n\n1. The script takes the path of a local bare repository and a work\n   directory from its caller. It uses `GitProgram` with the local\n   transport. It reads no Git credential.\n2. P1 borrows no deployment credential and no Gateway token. Your\n   reading of the sealed mint outcome is right: P1 has no such\n   outcome, so P1 makes no token.\n3. The owner of the room keeps the credential duty. With this script\n   the owner's own Git carries the branch from the local repository\n   to a Git host. State that in one sentence in the script's usage\n   text and in the P1 note.\n4. The P1 note names the limit: no publisher in P1 writes to a remote\n   Git host with a credential.\n\nThe delivery of an owner's credential to a publisher is a design\nquestion. It belongs to the P2 note, and I add it to that note's\nneeds. P1 does not wait for it.\n\nThis matches request bea87570: each of the nine witnesses uses a bare\nrepository and no network.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}